        {
          "id": "abe3b8f0-1f0f-47c3-ba12-7be602937b41",
          "name": "Salesforce Process Rules",
          "request": {
            "name": "Salesforce Process Rules",
            "description": {
              "content": "Returns a list of all active workflow rules. If a rule has actions, the actions will be listed under the rule. Can also be used to trigger all workflow rules that are associated with a specified record. The actions for a rule are only fired if the rule’s criteria is met. When using a POST request, if anything fails, the whole transaction is rolled back.\n\nCross-object workflow rules cannot be invoked using the REST API.\n\nTo get a list of the workflow rules or to trigger one or more workflow rules, the URI is: /vXX.X/process/rules/\nTo get the rules for a particular object: /vXX.X/process/rules/SObjectName\nTo get the metadata for a particular rule: /vXX.X/process/rules/SObjectName/workflowRuleId\nhttps://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_rest.meta/api_rest/resources_process_rules.htm",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "protocol": "https",
              "path": [
                "data",
                "v64.0",
                "process",
                "rules"
              ],
              "host": [
                "services"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": null
